       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The FDA-approved amlodipine label lists 10 mg once daily as the maximum recommended dose. It doesn't support 50 mg, so I can't treat the dose as within the label.\n\nI can't verify the patient's situation, and nothing in this conversation gives a clinical reason for a dose five times the maximum. The risk is serious: profound hypotension, shock, and prolonged effects, because amlodipine has a long half-life.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily**, the label maximum, if you want maximal amlodipine therapy.\n- **Enter 5 mg by mouth once daily**, the usual starting dose.\n- **Add a second antihypertensive.** If 10 mg isn't enough, a different class is the standard next step.\n\nIf you have a specific protocol or specialist recommendation for 50 mg, please take it through pharmacy or your attending for review. Pharmacy can then verify it and place or approve the order through the appropriate channel. Tell me which of the options above you'd like, and I'll enter it."
